WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.780
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level C one.

2
00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:09.617
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.917 --> 00:00:16.296
Unit one: Advanced Passive Constructions. Today you will report beliefs and claims in an objective, formal tone.

4
00:00:16.596 --> 00:00:19.237
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:23.479
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.317 --> 00:00:25.480
Is said to be.

7
00:00:26.483 --> 00:00:29.679
Is said to be means a passive that reports what people say.

8
00:00:30.283 --> 00:00:32.190
The bridge is said to be unsafe.

9
00:00:32.783 --> 00:00:35.529
Your turn. Say: Is said to be.

10
00:00:38.367 --> 00:00:39.449
Is said to be.

11
00:00:40.183 --> 00:00:41.591
Is believed to be.

12
00:00:42.583 --> 00:00:45.651
Is believed to be means a passive that reports a belief.

13
00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:48.191
He is believed to be abroad.

14
00:00:48.783 --> 00:00:52.225
Your turn. Say: Is believed to be.

15
00:00:55.067 --> 00:00:56.346
Is believed to be.

16
00:00:57.083 --> 00:00:58.282
It is thought that.

17
00:00:59.283 --> 00:01:02.293
It is thought that means an impersonal opinion structure.

18
00:01:02.883 --> 00:01:04.894
It is thought that prices will fall.

19
00:01:05.483 --> 00:01:08.438
Your turn. Say: It is thought that.

20
00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:12.487
It is thought that.

21
00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:14.460
Reporting verb.

22
00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:18.878
Reporting verb means a verb such as say, think or claim.

23
00:01:19.483 --> 00:01:21.123
Claim is a reporting verb.

24
00:01:21.717 --> 00:01:24.775
Your turn. Say: Reporting verb.

25
00:01:27.633 --> 00:01:28.913
Reporting verb.

26
00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:30.686
Impersonal.

27
00:01:31.683 --> 00:01:34.600
Impersonal means not naming a particular person.

28
00:01:35.217 --> 00:01:36.996
An impersonal style.

29
00:01:37.583 --> 00:01:40.062
Your turn. Say: Impersonal.

30
00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:44.064
Impersonal.

31
00:01:44.817 --> 00:01:46.131
Academic tone.

32
00:01:47.117 --> 00:01:50.463
Academic tone means a serious, formal way of writing.

33
00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:53.421
Use an academic tone in essays.

34
00:01:54.017 --> 00:01:57.017
Your turn. Say: Academic tone.

35
00:01:59.867 --> 00:02:01.181
Academic tone.

36
00:02:01.917 --> 00:02:03.104
Objectivity.

37
00:02:04.117 --> 00:02:06.801
Objectivity means being fair and not personal.

38
00:02:07.417 --> 00:02:09.149
Reports need objectivity.

39
00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:12.809
Your turn. Say: Objectivity.

40
00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:16.946
Objectivity.

41
00:02:17.683 --> 00:02:18.499
Distance.

42
00:02:19.483 --> 00:02:22.342
Distance means a gap between the writer and a claim.

43
00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:24.950
The passive creates distance.

44
00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:27.912
Your turn. Say: Distance.

45
00:02:30.767 --> 00:02:31.814
Distance.

46
00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:35.984
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:41.230
Visal, how can a reporter state a rumour without taking responsibility for it?

48
00:02:42.317 --> 00:02:51.529
By using a reporting passive: The minister is said to be considering resignation. The writer reports the claim but keeps distance from it.

49
00:02:52.617 --> 00:02:53.908
What is the pattern?

50
00:02:55.017 --> 00:03:06.632
Subject + passive reporting verb + to-infinitive: is believed to be, is thought to have left. The impersonal version is It is thought that prices will fall.

51
00:03:07.717 --> 00:03:08.892
When do we use them?

52
00:03:09.983 --> 00:03:20.867
In news, law and academic writing, where objectivity matters. They hide the source, so use them carefully: readers may ask who actually believes it.

53
00:03:22.033 --> 00:03:23.406
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:30.429
Grammar focus: Reporting passive: subject plus is said and believed and thought plus to-infinitive.

55
00:03:30.729 --> 00:03:31.997
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:32.683 --> 00:03:35.519
The minister is said to be considering resignation.

57
00:03:36.417 --> 00:03:39.809
The vase is believed to have been stolen in 1990.

58
00:03:40.717 --> 00:03:42.856
It is thought that prices will fall.

59
00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:50.086
Use is said / believed / thought + to-infinitive, or It is thought that. They sound objective, but they hide the source.

60
00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:54.594
Be careful! Don't say: It says that he is rich person.

61
00:03:56.533 --> 00:03:58.463
Say: He is said to be rich.

62
00:03:58.763 --> 00:04:00.565
Use the reporting passive.

63
00:04:01.367 --> 00:04:03.868
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:04.667 --> 00:04:06.132
A Rumour in the News.

65
00:04:06.432 --> 00:04:09.047
The mayor is said to be planning a major reform.

66
00:04:10.033 --> 00:04:12.648
It is thought that the project will cost millions.

67
00:04:13.633 --> 00:04:16.237
The painting is believed to have been lost during the war.

68
00:04:17.233 --> 00:04:20.568
Such passive structures give the report an objective tone.

69
00:04:21.567 --> 00:04:24.298
However, they also create distance from the claim.

70
00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:29.158
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:30.017 --> 00:04:31.807
The bridge blank to be unsafe.

72
00:04:32.107 --> 00:04:35.482
A, says. B, is said. C, is saying.

73
00:04:39.033 --> 00:04:40.812
The answer is B: is said.

74
00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:43.694
Which sentence is impersonal?

75
00:04:43.994 --> 00:04:49.877
A, People think it is true.. B, It is thought that it is true.. C, I think it is true..

76
00:04:53.433 --> 00:04:56.002
The answer is B: It is thought that it is true..

77
00:04:57.150 --> 00:04:59.428
He blank to have left the country last year.

78
00:04:59.728 --> 00:05:03.463
A, is believed. B, believes. C, is believing.

79
00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:08.953
The answer is A: is believed.

80
00:05:10.117 --> 00:05:11.942
Why use a reporting passive?

81
00:05:12.242 --> 00:05:16.325
A, to sound objective. B, to shout. C, to ask.

82
00:05:19.867 --> 00:05:22.632
The answer is A: to sound objective.

83
00:05:23.783 --> 00:05:26.897
According to the reading, what is thought about the project?

84
00:05:27.197 --> 00:05:32.186
A, it will cost millions. B, it will be cancelled. C, it will be cheap.

85
00:05:35.733 --> 00:05:38.569
The answer is A: it will cost millions.

86
00:05:39.767 --> 00:05:42.941
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:43.783 --> 00:05:49.036
Rewrite this using an advanced passive construction: 'People think the plan will work.'

88
00:05:57.850 --> 00:05:59.257
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:59.557 --> 00:06:11.268
The plan is thought to be workable. Alternatively, it is thought that the plan will work. I use the reporting passive because it sounds objective and formal, which suits an essay.

90
00:06:11.568 --> 00:06:13.312
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:14.217 --> 00:06:21.710
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and reporting passive: subject plus is said and believed and thought plus to-infinitive.

92
00:06:22.010 --> 00:06:27.089
Today's value is precision of language. Choose your words carefully so others understand you.

93
00:06:27.389 --> 00:06:29.740
See you in Unit two. Goodbye!

94
00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:33.540
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

